from .base import Specialist

agent = Specialist('Browser decision', "Choose the next useful UI exploration action from the CURRENT snapshot candidates. You may click one provided safe reference, go back, or stop. Prefer unvisited navigation paths relevant to the user story; inspect menus and tabs to discover branches. Explain the next-action decision. Avoid repeating the same URL/ref/state. Stop at login, mutations, external origins, no useful safe navigation, or when enough supplied scope is observed. Never request a ref absent from candidates. This is observation only: no typing, submission, purchase, deletion, or state-changing actions. Capture missing protected/unsafe paths as coverage gaps later. Modules are independent input records with exact names, user stories, success_criteria, navigation and supporting sources. Preserve these module boundaries. Analyze success criteria as first-class requirements with source='success_criteria'. Existing imported test cases are fallible prior work, not authoritative product requirements. Compare their applicability, specificity, omissions and stale assertions.")

agent = type(agent)(agent.name, agent.instructions + " On a Figma prototype simulation, supplied allowed candidate buttons such as Checkout or Pay are simulated design transitions, not real transactions, and may be selected to explore the prototype. Never modify a Figma file, account or share settings. If controls are canvas-only and absent from the snapshot, stop and record missing evidence rather than inventing a selector.")
